{
 "_notes": [
  "Discogs genres and styles for the canonical genre: vocabulary (TAG-077, TAG-078, ADR-0023). Keys starting with _ are comments.",
  "genres: the 15 Discogs genres in the fixed order of GEN-037. styles: lowercase style name to the genre Discogs files it under; one genre per style. A style Discogs also files under other genres is listed in also_under (GEN-039); the genre in styles is the first in the GEN-037 order, or a reviewed override (disco, new wave, acid jazz, gospel, rhythm and blues, dub and the older overrides of ADR-0021).",
  "Spelling: the name is Discogs's lowercased, except where the project already used another spelling (drum and bass, rock and roll, rhythm and blues, psytrance, synthpop, hi-nrg, hip house, euro disco, dance pop and the like): lookups ignore case, spaces, hyphens and '&' versus 'and', and one spelling is stored. discogs_names lists the names that differ beyond that.",
  "Source: the Discogs genres and styles list (support.discogs.com help article, Database Guidelines, Genres and Styles). Only names and the style to genre relation are used, no release data. The article is behind a bot check, so the list was written from memory of it and each style name was checked against the public Discogs database search (style=<name>, no token, 2026-10-16): a name is kept when releases with exactly that style exist. The style to genre relation cannot be read from the search (genre and style filter independently), so it comes from the reviewed table of ADR-0021 and the Discogs list as remembered; see README.md.",
  "unverified: names kept without a successful search check (see README.md); empty means every name was found in the Discogs database."
 ],
